{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfef3QdJidyQfmAsGNRCt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've written the candidate `balance_aware_length_scaled_ideal` and it passed the self-check (`OK`). In a short test fit (1 chain, 100 draws) its ELPD-LOO was −1069.7, about level with the incumbent's −1069.9 — so it fits roughly as well, but a smoke fit can't show whether it's better. The check doesn't test novelty, convergence or speed; those are only tested at admission.\n\n**The one change:** it keeps the incumbent `length_scaled_alternation_ideal` as it is and adds one shared penalty for how lopsided a sequence's heads/tails count is. The penalty is the squared gap between its share of heads and one half. I took this from the global-balance part of `local_representativeness`.\n\n**Why this change:** the critique's one significant finding was `shorter_longest_run_pref` (observed 0.588 vs 0.448 predicted, p = 0.018). It says that when two sequences have the same number of switches, people prefer the one with the shorter longest run more than the model predicts. I took that statistic and offered a different explanation from a streak penalty. With equal switches, the sequence with the longer run is usually the less balanced one (e.g. HHHHTT vs HHHTTT). Two streak-penalty variants are already in the set (`periodic_ideal_absolute_streak_penalty` and `length_scaled_alternation_ideal_streak`), and neither beats the incumbent. Balance is also a different claim from a streak penalty, so it should differ enough from the live models to pass the novelty gate, though that hasn't been checked yet. Note that the FDR-adjusted q is 0.144, so the critique finding itself is only exploratory.\n\n**One warning from the check:** PSIS-LOO came out unreliable, with 5.1% of trials having Pareto k > 0.5, against a 1% tolerance. If that holds in admission's full fit, this model's ELPD-LOO estimate may not be trusted when it is ranked.\n\nAll three files are in `iter_3/candidate_3/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3257,"cache_read_input_tokens":64188,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3257,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fda3532b-7fd4-4bcb-818c-ebdc0e8fb826","uuid":"702ec950-a5d6-4020-9756-723cf09b83f9","timestamp":"2026-10-03T04:16:23.821Z","request_id":"req_011Cfef3QEjkR5TSuufZkj3B"}
